module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.DirectSum.Internal
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.GroupWithZero.Finset
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.GradedAlgebra.HomogeneousLocalization
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.GradedAlgebra.RingHom
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.BigOperators

/-!
# One degree for all the generators of a localized kernel

Let `φ : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ` be a homomorphism of `ℕ`-graded rings and let `f ∈ 𝒜 e` be homogeneous of
positive degree. The degree-zero localization `HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 f` is the ring of
fractions `a / f ^ n` with `a` homogeneous of degree `n • e`, and `φ` induces a map of those
localizations whose kernel is an ideal of `Away 𝒜 f`. This file answers: **when that kernel is
finitely generated, can its generators be taken to be fractions whose numerators all have one
and the same degree, and can that degree be chosen uniformly over a finite family of `f`'s?**

The answer is yes, and the mechanism is the one the Stacks Project uses in the proof of Tag
0802: `f` is invertible on the locus where the fraction lives, so a numerator `a` of degree
`n • e` may be replaced by `a * f ^ m`, of degree `(n + m) • e`, without changing the fraction
(`awayMk_mul_pow`), and multiplying a generating family by units does not change the ideal it
spans (`span_range_mul_units`). Raising every numerator to a common exponent therefore levels
the degrees of the generators for one `f`, and taking a common multiple of the degrees of the
members of a finite family levels them across the family. Because any multiple of a working
degree works again, the degrees coming from different members can afterwards be merged, which is
what `exists_uniform_degree_kernel_generators_multiple` records.

Also proved here is the description of membership in the ideal spanned by a family of
degree-`d` elements: in degree `d + k` such a membership is exactly a finite sum of products of
family members with degree-`k` coefficients (`mem_span_range_homogeneous_iff`), and below degree
`d` it forces the element to vanish (`eq_zero_of_mem_span_range_of_lt_degree`). This is the
algebraic content of "the ideal generated by a submodule sitting in a single degree".

## Main results

* `Stacks.RingTheory.UniformDegreeKernel.awayMk_mul_pow`: multiplying numerator and denominator
  by a power of `f` does not change a fraction in `HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 f`.
* `Stacks.RingTheory.UniformDegreeKernel.awayMk_eq_zero_iff`: such a fraction vanishes exactly
  when a power of `f` annihilates its numerator.
* `Stacks.RingTheory.UniformDegreeKernel.exists_homogeneous_numerator_in_kernel`: an element of
  the kernel has a numerator of positive denominator-exponent which `φ` itself kills.
* `Stacks.RingTheory.UniformDegreeKernel.exists_common_degree_kernel_generators`: a finitely
  generated localized kernel is spanned by fractions whose numerators all have one degree and
  are all killed by `φ`.
* `Stacks.RingTheory.UniformDegreeKernel.exists_uniform_degree_kernel_generators` and
  `exists_uniform_degree_kernel_generators_multiple`: one degree, and then every multiple of it,
  works simultaneously for a finite family of positive-degree homogeneous elements.
* `Stacks.RingTheory.UniformDegreeKernel.bijective_awayMap`: a degreewise surjective `φ` whose
  kernel is annihilated degreewise by powers of `f` induces an isomorphism of the degree-zero
  localizations away from `f`.
* `Stacks.RingTheory.UniformDegreeKernel.mem_span_range_homogeneous_iff` and
  `eq_zero_of_mem_span_range_of_lt_degree`: the degreewise description of the ideal spanned by a
  family concentrated in one degree.

## Implementation notes

The degree of a numerator is written `n • e` rather than `n * e` throughout, because that is the
indexing `HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk` uses, and `add_nsmul` is what splits it when an
exponent is added. Where an exponent has to be increased to a common value, the difference is
introduced by `Nat.add_sub_of_le` and the degree hypothesis is transported by `simpa only`
rather than rewritten, since the degree occurs in the type of the membership proof that
`HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk` takes as an argument.

Nothing here carries a `@[stacks 0802]` attribute. Tag 0802 is a statement about a closed
subscheme of a relative `Proj` over a quasi-compact quasi-separated base: it asserts the
existence of a positive degree `d` and a quasi-coherent finite type submodule
`ℱ ⊆ 𝒜_d` with `Z = Proj_S(𝒜/ℱ𝒜)`. What is proved below is the graded-ring step of its proof —
the choice of the common degree `d` — for a homomorphism of graded rings which is a variable,
with no base scheme and no closed immersion in sight. Those are hypotheses the tag does not
have, so the tag is not claimed.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0802](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0802)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Stacks.RingTheory.UniformDegreeKernel

/-- **Membership in the ideal spanned by a family concentrated in degree `d`, read in degree
`d + k`.** A homogeneous element of degree `d + k` lies in the ideal spanned by a family of
degree-`d` elements exactly when it is a finite sum of products of family members with
degree-`k` coefficients. -/
theorem mem_span_range_homogeneous_iff
    {A σ T : Type*} [CommSemiring A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubmonoidClass σ A]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] (d k : ℕ)
    (f : T → A) (hf : ∀ t, f t ∈ 𝒜 d) {a : A} (ha : a ∈ 𝒜 (d + k)) :
    a ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range f) ↔
      ∃ (t : Finset T) (c : T → 𝒜 k), a = ∑ x ∈ t, f x * c x := by
  classical
  constructor
  · intro h
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Finsupp.mem_span_range_iff_exists_finsupp.mp h
    refine ⟨c.support, fun x => DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 (c x) k, ?_⟩
    have hproj := congrArg (GradedRing.proj 𝒜 (d + k)) hc
    have hap : GradedRing.proj 𝒜 (d + k) a = a :=
      DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒜 ha
    rw [hap, Finsupp.sum, map_sum] at hproj
    rw [← hproj]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun x _ => ?_
    show (DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 (c x * f x) (d + k) : A) = _
    rw [mul_comm (c x), DirectSum.coe_decompose_mul_add_of_left_mem 𝒜 (hf x)]
  · rintro ⟨t, c, rfl⟩
    exact Ideal.sum_mem _ fun x hx =>
      Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_range_self (x := x))

/-- **The ideal spanned by a family concentrated in degree `d` has nothing below degree `d`.**
A homogeneous element of degree less than `d` lying in that ideal is zero. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_mem_span_range_of_lt_degree
    {A σ T : Type*} [CommSemiring A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubmonoidClass σ A]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] {d n : ℕ}
    (f : T → A) (hf : ∀ t, f t ∈ 𝒜 d) (hnd : n < d)
    {a : A} (ha : a ∈ 𝒜 n) (h : a ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range f)) : a = 0 := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Finsupp.mem_span_range_iff_exists_finsupp.mp h
  have hproj := congrArg (GradedRing.proj 𝒜 n) hc
  have hap : GradedRing.proj 𝒜 n a = a :=
    DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒜 ha
  rw [hap, Finsupp.sum, map_sum] at hproj
  rw [← hproj]
  refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun x _ => ?_
  show (DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 (c x * f x) n : A) = 0
  rw [DirectSum.coe_decompose_mul_of_right_mem 𝒜 n (hf x),
    ite_eq_right (Nat.not_le.mpr hnd)]

/-- **Multiplying a generating family by units does not change the ideal it spans.** This is why
a numerator may be multiplied by a power of the localizing element: that power is a unit in the
localization. -/
theorem span_range_mul_units
    {A T : Type*} [CommSemiring A] (f v : T → A) (hv : ∀ t, IsUnit (v t)) :
    Ideal.span (Set.range (fun t => f t * v t)) = Ideal.span (Set.range f) := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · apply Ideal.span_le.mpr
    rintro _ ⟨t, rfl⟩
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_range_self (x := t))
  · apply Ideal.span_le.mpr
    rintro _ ⟨t, rfl⟩
    exact (Ideal.mul_unit_mem_iff_mem _ (hv t)).mp
      (Ideal.mem_span_range_self (x := t))

/-- **A common multiple of a finite family of positive integers, with a prescribed lower bound on
each cofactor.** For every member `x` of a finite set the common multiple is `n x * m` for some
`m` at least `e x`. This is the choice of `d` in the proof of Tag 0802: a common multiple of the
degrees, large enough that the exponent each generator has to be raised to is nonnegative. -/
theorem exists_common_multiple_ge
    {T : Type*} (t : Finset T) (n e : T → ℕ) (hn : ∀ x ∈ t, 0 < n x) :
    ∃ d : ℕ, 0 < d ∧ ∀ x ∈ t, ∃ m : ℕ, e x ≤ m ∧ d = n x * m := by
  classical
  let p := ∏ x ∈ t, n x
  let b := t.sup e + 1
  have hp : 0 < p := Finset.prod_pos hn
  refine ⟨p * b, Nat.mul_pos hp (Nat.zero_lt_succ _), ?_⟩
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ : n x ∣ p := Finset.dvd_prod_of_mem n hx
  have hqpos : 0 < q := Nat.pos_of_ne_zero fun h => by simp [hq, h] at hp
  refine ⟨q * b, (Nat.le_succ_of_le (Finset.le_sup hx)).trans (Nat.le_mul_of_pos_left b hqpos), ?_⟩
  rw [hq, Nat.mul_assoc]

/-- **Raising the denominator exponent of a fraction.** Multiplying numerator and denominator of
`a / f ^ n` by `f ^ m` gives the same element of `HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 f`. -/
theorem awayMk_mul_pow
    {A σ : Type*} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] {f : A} {d : ℕ} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d)
    (n m : ℕ) (a : A) (ha : a ∈ 𝒜 (n • d))
    (ha' : a * f ^ m ∈ 𝒜 ((n + m) • d)) :
    HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk 𝒜 hf (n + m) (a * f ^ m) ha' =
      HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk 𝒜 hf n a ha := by
  apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
  rw [HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk, HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk]
  simp only [Localization.mk_eq_mk']
  convert IsLocalization.mk'_cancel (S := Localization (Submonoid.powers f)) a
    (⟨f ^ n, ⟨n, rfl⟩⟩ : Submonoid.powers f)
    (⟨f ^ m, ⟨m, rfl⟩⟩ : Submonoid.powers f) using 1
  simp only [pow_add]
  rfl

/-- Multiplying a degree `n • d` element by `f ^ m` gives degree `(n + m) • d`. -/
private theorem mul_pow_mem_graded_add
    {A σ : Type*} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] {f : A} {d : ℕ} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d)
    {n : ℕ} (m : ℕ) {a : A} (ha : a ∈ 𝒜 (n • d)) : a * f ^ m ∈ 𝒜 ((n + m) • d) := by
  simpa only [add_nsmul] using SetLike.mul_mem_graded ha (SetLike.pow_mem_graded m hf)

/-- Multiplying a degree `n • d` element by `f ^ (N - n)` raises its degree to `N • d`. -/
private theorem mul_pow_sub_mem_graded
    {A σ : Type*} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] {f : A} {d : ℕ} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d)
    {n N : ℕ} (hnN : n ≤ N) {a : A} (ha : a ∈ 𝒜 (n • d)) : a * f ^ (N - n) ∈ 𝒜 (N • d) := by
  simpa only [Nat.add_sub_of_le hnN] using mul_pow_mem_graded_add 𝒜 hf (N - n) ha

/-- Raising the denominator exponent of a fraction from `n` up to `N`. -/
private theorem awayMk_mul_pow_sub
    {A σ : Type*} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] {f : A} {d : ℕ} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d)
    {n N : ℕ} (hnN : n ≤ N) (a : A) (ha : a ∈ 𝒜 (n • d)) :
    HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk 𝒜 hf N (a * f ^ (N - n))
        (mul_pow_sub_mem_graded 𝒜 hf hnN ha) =
      HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk 𝒜 hf n a ha := by
  simpa only [Nat.add_sub_of_le hnN] using
    awayMk_mul_pow 𝒜 hf n (N - n) a ha (mul_pow_mem_graded_add 𝒜 hf (N - n) ha)

/-- **When a fraction vanishes.** The element `a / f ^ n` of
`HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 f` is zero exactly when some power of `f` annihilates `a`. -/
theorem awayMk_eq_zero_iff
    {A σ : Type*} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] {f : A} {d : ℕ} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d)
    (n : ℕ) (a : A) (ha : a ∈ 𝒜 (n • d)) :
    HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk 𝒜 hf n a ha = 0 ↔ ∃ k : ℕ, f ^ k * a = 0 := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    have h' := congrArg HomogeneousLocalization.val h
    rw [HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk, HomogeneousLocalization.val_zero,
      Localization.mk_eq_mk'] at h'
    obtain ⟨⟨_, ⟨k, rfl⟩⟩, hk⟩ := (IsLocalization.mk'_eq_zero_iff _ _).mp h'
    exact ⟨k, hk⟩
  · rintro ⟨k, hk⟩
    apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
    rw [HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk, HomogeneousLocalization.val_zero,
      Localization.mk_eq_mk']
    exact (IsLocalization.mk'_eq_zero_iff _ _).mpr ⟨⟨f ^ k, ⟨k, rfl⟩⟩, hk⟩

/-- **A numerator that `φ` itself kills.** An element of the kernel of the induced map of
degree-zero localizations away from `f` can be written as `a / f ^ n` with `n > 0`, `a`
homogeneous of degree `n • d`, and `φ a = 0`: the failure of `φ a` to vanish on the nose is
absorbed into a power of `f`. -/
theorem exists_homogeneous_numerator_in_kernel
    {A B σ τ : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A] [SetLike τ B] [AddSubgroupClass τ B]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) (ℬ : ℕ → τ) [GradedRing 𝒜] [GradedRing ℬ]
    (φ : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ) {f : A} {d : ℕ} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d)
    (z : HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 f)
    (hz : HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map φ f z = 0) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (a : A) (ha : a ∈ 𝒜 (n • d)),
      0 < n ∧ φ a = 0 ∧ HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk 𝒜 hf n a ha = z := by
  obtain ⟨n, a, ha, rfl⟩ := HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk_surjective 𝒜 hf z
  have hz' := congrArg HomogeneousLocalization.val hz
  simp only [HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map_mk, HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk,
    HomogeneousLocalization.val_zero, Localization.mk_eq_mk'] at hz'
  obtain ⟨⟨_, ⟨m, rfl⟩⟩, hm⟩ := (IsLocalization.mk'_eq_zero_iff _ _).mp hz'
  have ha' := mul_pow_mem_graded_add 𝒜 hf (m + 1) ha
  refine ⟨n + (m + 1), a * f ^ (m + 1), ha', by omega, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [map_mul, map_pow, pow_succ]
    show φ a * (φ f ^ m * φ f) = 0
    rw [← mul_assoc, mul_comm (φ a) (φ f ^ m), hm, zero_mul]
  · exact awayMk_mul_pow 𝒜 hf n (m + 1) a ha ha'

/-- **One degree for all the generators, for a single `f`.** If the kernel of the induced map of
degree-zero localizations away from `f` is finitely generated, it is spanned by finitely many
fractions whose numerators all have the same degree `N • d` with `N > 0` and are all killed by
`φ`. -/
theorem exists_common_degree_kernel_generators
    {A B σ τ : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A] [SetLike τ B] [AddSubgroupClass τ B]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) (ℬ : ℕ → τ) [GradedRing 𝒜] [GradedRing ℬ]
    (φ : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ) {f : A} {d : ℕ} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d)
    (hfg : (RingHom.ker (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map φ f)).FG) :
    ∃ (N : ℕ) (t : Finset (HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 f)) (a : t → A)
      (ha : ∀ x, a x ∈ 𝒜 (N • d)),
      0 < N ∧ (∀ x, φ (a x) = 0) ∧
      (∀ x, HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk 𝒜 hf N (a x) (ha x) = x.val) ∧
      Ideal.span (t : Set (HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 f)) =
        RingHom.ker (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map φ f) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hfg
  have htker (x : t) : HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map φ f x.val = 0 :=
    RingHom.mem_ker.mp (ht ▸ Ideal.subset_span x.property)
  choose n a ha hn hφ heq using fun x : t =>
    exists_homogeneous_numerator_in_kernel 𝒜 ℬ φ hf x.val (htker x)
  let N := Finset.univ.sup n + 1
  have hnle (x : t) : n x ≤ N :=
    Nat.le_succ_of_le (Finset.le_sup (Finset.mem_univ x))
  let b : t → A := fun x => a x * f ^ (N - n x)
  have hb (x : t) : b x ∈ 𝒜 (N • d) := mul_pow_sub_mem_graded 𝒜 hf (hnle x) (ha x)
  refine ⟨N, t, b, hb, Nat.zero_lt_succ _, ?_, ?_, ht⟩
  · intro x
    simp only [b, map_mul, map_pow, hφ, zero_mul]
  · intro x
    exact (awayMk_mul_pow_sub 𝒜 hf (hnle x) (a x) (ha x)).trans (heq x)

/-- **A degreewise surjective homomorphism of graded rings whose kernel is annihilated, in every
degree, by a power of `f` induces an isomorphism of degree-zero localizations away from `f`.** -/
theorem bijective_awayMap
    {A B σ τ : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A] [SetLike τ B] [AddSubgroupClass τ B]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) (ℬ : ℕ → τ) [GradedRing 𝒜] [GradedRing ℬ]
    (φ : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ) {f : A} {d : ℕ} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d)
    (hsurj : ∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), b ∈ ℬ n → ∃ a ∈ 𝒜 n, φ a = b)
    (hker : ∀ (j : ℕ) (a : A), a ∈ 𝒜 (j * d) → φ a = 0 → ∃ k : ℕ, f ^ k * a = 0) :
    Function.Bijective (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map φ f) := by
  constructor
  · intro z w hzw
    rw [← sub_eq_zero, ← map_sub] at hzw
    rw [← sub_eq_zero]
    obtain ⟨n, a, ha, hmk⟩ := HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk_surjective 𝒜 hf (z - w)
    rw [← hmk] at hzw ⊢
    rw [HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map_mk,
      awayMk_eq_zero_iff ℬ (GradedRingHom.map_mem φ hf) n (φ a)
        (GradedRingHom.map_mem φ ha)] at hzw
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hzw
    have hφ : φ ((f : A) ^ m * a) = 0 := by
      rw [map_mul, map_pow]
      exact hm
    have hmem : (f : A) ^ m * a ∈ 𝒜 ((m + n) * d) := by
      simpa only [add_mul, smul_eq_mul] using
        SetLike.mul_mem_graded (SetLike.pow_mem_graded m hf) ha
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hker _ _ hmem hφ
    rw [awayMk_eq_zero_iff 𝒜 hf n a ha]
    refine ⟨k + m, ?_⟩
    rw [pow_add, mul_assoc, hk]
  · intro z
    obtain ⟨n, b, hb, hmk⟩ :=
      HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk_surjective ℬ (GradedRingHom.map_mem φ hf) z
    obtain ⟨a, ha, hab⟩ := hsurj (n • d) b hb
    refine ⟨HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk 𝒜 hf n a ha, ?_⟩
    rw [HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map_mk, ← hmk]
    apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
    rw [HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk, HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk, hab]
    rfl

/-- **One degree for a whole finite family.** Given finitely many homogeneous elements of
positive degree, each with finitely generated localized kernel, there is a single positive
degree `D` such that for every member the localized kernel is spanned by fractions whose
numerators are homogeneous of degree `D` and are killed by `φ`. The degree of the member divides
`D`, and the denominator exponent is the cofactor. -/
theorem exists_uniform_degree_kernel_generators
    {A B σ τ : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
    [SetLike τ B] [AddSubgroupClass τ B]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) (ℬ : ℕ → τ) [GradedRing 𝒜] [GradedRing ℬ]
    (φ : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ) (S : Finset (Σ n : ℕ, 𝒜 n))
    (hS : ∀ x ∈ S, 0 < x.1)
    (hfg : ∀ x ∈ S,
      (RingHom.ker (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map φ x.2.1)).FG) :
    ∃ D : ℕ, 0 < D ∧ ∀ x : S, ∃ e : ℕ, D = e * x.val.1 ∧
      ∃ (t : Finset (HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 x.val.2.1)) (a : t → A)
        (ha : ∀ y, a y ∈ 𝒜 (e • x.val.1)),
        (∀ y, φ (a y) = 0) ∧
        (∀ y, HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk 𝒜 x.val.2.2 e (a y) (ha y) = y.val) ∧
        Ideal.span (t : Set (HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 x.val.2.1)) =
          RingHom.ker (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map φ x.val.2.1) := by
  classical
  have hlocal (x : S) := exists_common_degree_kernel_generators
    𝒜 ℬ φ x.val.2.2 (hfg x.val x.property)
  choose N t a ha hN hφ hmk hspan using hlocal
  obtain ⟨D, hD, hmultiple⟩ := exists_common_multiple_ge Finset.univ
    (fun x : S => x.val.1) N (fun x _ => hS x.val x.property)
  have hm (x : S) : ∃ e : ℕ, N x ≤ e ∧ D = x.val.1 * e :=
    hmultiple x (Finset.mem_univ x)
  choose e he hde using hm
  refine ⟨D, hD, ?_⟩
  intro x
  let b : t x → A := fun y => a x y * (x.val.2.1 : A) ^ (e x - N x)
  have hb (y : t x) : b y ∈ 𝒜 (e x • x.val.1) :=
    mul_pow_sub_mem_graded 𝒜 x.val.2.2 (he x) (ha x y)
  refine ⟨e x, by simpa only [mul_comm] using hde x,
    t x, b, hb, ?_, ?_, hspan x⟩
  · intro y
    simp only [b, map_mul, map_pow, hφ x y, zero_mul]
  · intro y
    exact (awayMk_mul_pow_sub 𝒜 x.val.2.2 (he x) (a x y) (ha x y)).trans (hmk x y)

/-- **Every multiple of a working degree works again.** The same statement as
`exists_uniform_degree_kernel_generators`, but asserted for every positive multiple `D'` of the
degree `D` produced there. This is the form in which the degrees obtained separately on the
members of a cover can be merged into one: take a common multiple. -/
theorem exists_uniform_degree_kernel_generators_multiple
    {A B σ τ : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
    [SetLike τ B] [AddSubgroupClass τ B]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) (ℬ : ℕ → τ) [GradedRing 𝒜] [GradedRing ℬ]
    (φ : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ) (S : Finset (Σ n : ℕ, 𝒜 n))
    (hS : ∀ x ∈ S, 0 < x.1)
    (hfg : ∀ x ∈ S,
      (RingHom.ker (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map φ x.2.1)).FG) :
    ∃ D : ℕ, 0 < D ∧ ∀ D' : ℕ, D ∣ D' → 0 < D' → ∀ x : S, ∃ e : ℕ, D' = e * x.val.1 ∧
      ∃ (t : Finset (HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 x.val.2.1)) (a : t → A)
        (ha : ∀ y, a y ∈ 𝒜 (e • x.val.1)),
        (∀ y, φ (a y) = 0) ∧
        (∀ y, HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk 𝒜 x.val.2.2 e (a y) (ha y) = y.val) ∧
        Ideal.span (t : Set (HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 x.val.2.1)) =
          RingHom.ker (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map φ x.val.2.1) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨D, hD, hdata⟩ :=
    exists_uniform_degree_kernel_generators 𝒜 ℬ φ S hS hfg
  refine ⟨D, hD, ?_⟩
  intro D' hdvd hD' x
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hdvd
  have hcpos : 0 < c := by
    rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos c with h | h
    · simp [h, hc] at hD'
    · exact h
  obtain ⟨e, hde, t, a, ha, hφ, hmk, hspan⟩ := hdata x
  have hepos : 0 < e := by
    rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos e with h | h
    · simp [h, hde] at hD
    · exact h
  have hle : e ≤ c * e := Nat.le_mul_of_pos_left e hcpos
  have hmem (y : t) : a y * (x.val.2.1 : A) ^ (c * e - e) ∈ 𝒜 ((c * e) • x.val.1) :=
    mul_pow_sub_mem_graded 𝒜 x.val.2.2 hle (ha y)
  refine ⟨c * e, by rw [hc, hde]; ring, t,
    fun y => a y * (x.val.2.1 : A) ^ (c * e - e), hmem, ?_, ?_, hspan⟩
  · intro y
    simp only [map_mul, map_pow, hφ y, zero_mul]
  · intro y
    exact (awayMk_mul_pow_sub 𝒜 x.val.2.2 hle (a y) (ha y)).trans (hmk y)

/-- **Packaging a finite set of homogeneous elements with their degrees.** A finite set of ring
elements, each homogeneous of some positive degree, is the image of a finite set of
degree-tagged homogeneous elements. This is the form
`exists_uniform_degree_kernel_generators` consumes. -/
theorem exists_homogeneous_finset_lift
    {A σ : Type*} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) (t : Finset A)
    (ht : ∀ f ∈ t, ∃ n : ℕ, 0 < n ∧ f ∈ 𝒜 n) :
    ∃ S : Finset (Σ n : ℕ, 𝒜 n),
      (∀ x ∈ S, 0 < x.1) ∧
      (∀ f ∈ t, ∃ x ∈ S, (x.2 : A) = f) ∧
      (∀ x ∈ S, (x.2 : A) ∈ t) := by
  classical
  have h : ∀ f : t, ∃ n : ℕ, 0 < n ∧ (f.1 : A) ∈ 𝒜 n :=
    fun f => ht f.1 f.2
  choose n hn hmem using h
  let lift (f : t) : Σ n : ℕ, 𝒜 n := ⟨n f, ⟨f.1, hmem f⟩⟩
  refine ⟨Finset.univ.image lift, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rintro x hx
    obtain ⟨f, _, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hx
    exact hn f
  · intro f hf
    exact ⟨lift ⟨f, hf⟩, Finset.mem_image.mpr
      ⟨⟨f, hf⟩, Finset.mem_univ _, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
  · rintro x hx
    obtain ⟨f, _, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hx
    exact f.2

end Stacks.RingTheory.UniformDegreeKernel

